`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Infrastructure"}),": Claude access for people who are not engineers (claude.ai or Cowork); an agreed ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"intent.md"})," template; a shared, version-controlled home for intent that the product owner watches. For a single product the simplest home is an ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"intent/"})," folder in the product repo. This setup keeps the artifact chain next to the code derived from it. A dedicated intent repo is only worth the overhead when intent spans many repositories, and in a monorepo it is a directory. The Legacy systems section in ",(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Stage 3: Build"})," covers how this home relates to a Jira or requirements tool that already holds the record."]}),`
